From 4a4e1e3c2166e6c57397fdc98565895ad38e7914 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:58:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Preserve verified runtime termination after failed
 receipts

Separate expiry termination permission from strict modern-result closure. TTL and max-runtime may terminate only a birth-verified outer worker; the post-kill gate still reserves closure and accounting for the atomic finalizer after every historical binding exits.

Proof: canonical runtime regression RED 8 passed/2 failed before implementation, GREEN with real hung writers; 1264 tests across 11 focused/scanner files plus existing expiry suites. No existing tests changed, no live process signals, no production deployment.
---
